course: dictionary
lesson: 12886
title: The entrant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An entrant is a person, team or animal that enters a competition, race or exam. When you sign up for a race, a spelling bee or a test, you become an entrant. «Forty entrants lined up at the start of the race.»
explain: The word comes from the verb enter, so an entrant is someone who goes in. A newcomer can be an entrant too: «She is a new entrant to the school this term.» Here it means someone who has just joined.
explain: In maths problems, the number of entrants tells you how many people take part. Look for clue words such as «each», «new» or «youngest» to see which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: An entrant is a person, team or animal that enters a competition, race or exam.
fact: Entrant comes from the verb enter, which means to go in or to join.
fact: «Each entrant» means every one of the people taking part.
fact: «New entrants» means people who have just joined, such as a new school or job.
fact: In a maths problem, the number of entrants is how many people take part.
exercise: «Eight entrants signed up for the spelling bee.» What is an entrant? | A referee who blows the whistle | A rule about the start line | *A person who enters a race or contest | A prize for the winner
exercise: In a maths contest, «There were 20 entrants, and half of them were girls.» How many girls were entrants? | 40 | 2 | 20 | *10
exercise: «She was the youngest entrant in the swimming race.» What does entrant mean here? | A coach who gives out drinks | A lifeguard who watches the pool | *A person taking part in the race | A medal for the fastest swim
test: «Each entrant must be under twelve to join the junior race.» What does «each entrant» mean? | *Every person who enters the race | The people who watch the race | The coach of the team | Only the winner
test: Which word means a person who has just joined a school or a job? | *Entrant | Champion | Judge | Referee
exam: Which of these can be an entrant? | A rock that sits in the park | *A dog that enters a dog show | A sandwich in a lunchbox | A cloud that drifts over the hill
